// opencode.local.example.jsonc — machine-local OpenCode overrides.
//
// To use: copy this file to the location your local machine's opencode.jsonc
// can pick up. OpenCode currently loads a single config file from
// ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc, so machine-local additions need to
// be merged into that file after stowing, OR kept in a separate local copy.
//
// This file is NOT committed to the dotfiles repo — it documents
// machine-specific additions that are too local to belong in shared config.
//
// Example: re-add the workstation-only opencode-plan-annotator plugin
// if you have the project checked out at ~/projects/opencode-plan-anotator/.
//
// Add the following entry to your "plugin" array:
//
//   "file://~/.config/opencode/plugin/annotate-plan.ts"
//
// The annotate-plan.ts plugin itself now uses Deno.env.get("HOME") internally
// so it is portable once loaded from any machine that has the project checked out.
